; The root actions, then four actions for IntegrationParser (Tests/Integration/Parser/FMTActionParser.cpp):
; two age conditions written with the strict operators > and <, and the same conditions written
; with >= and <=. Woodstock refuses > and < (messages 142 and 143 of Wk.msg); FMT reads them
; without their bound (Tests/ETAT.md, section 2.7).
*ACTION aFire N
*OPERABLE AFire
? prod ? _AGE >= 1

*ACTION arecup Y
*OPERABLE arecup
? feu ? volumetotal >= 100

*ACTION COUPEtotale Y CT
*OPERABLE COUPEtotale
? prod ? volumetotal >= 100

*ACTION aCaribou N Massif protection du caribou
*OPERABLE aCaribou
UC prod ? _AGE >= 8

*ACTION plantation Y _LOCKEXEMPT
*OPERABLE plantation
;c'est rendu dans chacun des scenario de replanning - > ? pourpl ? _AGE = 0 ;_AGE >= 1 AND _AGE <= 3
? prod ? _AGE >= 1 AND _AGE <= 3

*ACTION aOlderThan Y
*OPERABLE aOlderThan
? prod ? _AGE > 10

*ACTION aFromAge Y
*OPERABLE aFromAge
? prod ? _AGE >= 11

*ACTION aYoungerThan Y
*OPERABLE aYoungerThan
? prod ? _AGE < 5

*ACTION aUpToAge Y
*OPERABLE aUpToAge
? prod ? _AGE <= 4
